---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/contact';
import { UNREVIEWED_PAGES } from '../lib/seo/unreviewed-pages';

const path = '/about';
// OWNER: fill the {{PLACEHOLDERS}} below, then remove '/about' from UNREVIEWED_PAGES
// (src/lib/seo/unreviewed-pages.ts) to index this page. While it is in that set the page is noindex and
// out of the sitemap; src/lib/seo/unreviewed-pages.test.ts fails if a page with placeholders is not in it.
// Confirm every claim here is true of how you actually operate before publishing.
const PH = {
  name: '{{FOUNDER_NAME}}',
  bio: '{{FOUNDER_BIO}}',
  photo: '{{FOUNDER_PHOTO}}',
  vetting: '{{VETTING_CRITERIA}}',
};
---
<BaseLayout title="About RayValue" description="RayValue is an independent solar and battery payback site for homeowners worldwide: who it is for, how it is funded and how we keep it honest." path={path} noindex={UNREVIEWED_PAGES.has(path)}>
  <PageHero title="An independent solar payback site, country by country" titleId="about-title">
    <Breadcrumbs slot="crumbs" tone="dark" items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
    RayValue helps homeowners work out what solar panels and home batteries are worth where they live, using their own country&rsquo;s tariffs, export rules and incentives. It is not affiliated with any utility, installer or government agency.
  </PageHero>

  <div class="page !pt-8">
    {!PH.name.startsWith('{{') && (
      <>
        <h2>Who runs RayValue</h2>
        <p><strong>{PH.name}</strong></p>
        {!PH.bio.startsWith('{{') && <p>{PH.bio}</p>}
        {!PH.photo.startsWith('{{') && <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">Photo: {PH.photo}</p>}
      </>
    )}

    <h2 class="!mt-0">Why RayValue exists</h2>
    <p>
      Solar maths depends on rules that differ in every country and change often: price caps, export payments, net metering,
      rebates, VAT and tax treatment. Many online estimates ignore that, or assume an incentive that has already ended. RayValue
      exists to show what rooftop solar and batteries are worth <em>today</em>, in your country, as honest low, likely and high
      ranges instead of one hopeful number.
    </p>

    <h2>What you will find here</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
      <li><strong>Calculators</strong> for the countries where we have enough verified data to build one. The list is on the <a href="/#calculators">home page</a> and grows as new countries are verified.</li>
      <li><strong>Country guides and blog posts</strong> on tariffs, rebates, deadlines and costs, each listing its sources. Browse <a href="/guides">guides</a> and the <a href="/blog">blog</a> for every country, or pick a country on the <a href="/#countries">home page</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Local pages</strong> for cities, regions and utilities where we hold sourced local data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we keep it honest</h2>
    <p>
      Every rate, cost and statistic is stored with the URL of its source and the date we last checked it. Our own modelling
      choices are labelled as assumptions with the reasoning behind them. If we cannot verify a number we leave it out. Sources
      are re-read on a schedule, and a figure only counts as confirmed while the source still supports it. The details are on the{' '}
      <a href="/methodology">methodology</a> page.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our editorial stance is to cover both sides. Articles explain the case for solar and the case against: when it pays
      back, when it does not, what a battery adds and what it costs, and where the rules are changing in ways that count against
      you. Offers and affiliate links never feed the calculator numbers.
    </p>

    <h2>How RayValue makes money</h2>
    <p>
      The calculators and guides are free and you do not need to sign up to see results. Some links on the site are affiliate
      links, which can earn a commission at no extra cost to you; they are always marked. In the United States, installers
      can pay RayValue for introductions to homeowners who ask to hear from them. Neither changes the numbers in an estimate.
      Details are on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> page.
    </p>

    {!PH.vetting.startsWith('{{') && (
      <>
        <h2>How installers are vetted</h2>
        <p>{PH.vetting}</p>
      </>
    )}
    <p>
      When you request quotes (a US-only feature), your details are shared only with up to 3 installers serving your area, as
      described in the consent you agree to, and you can ask us to delete them at any time. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    {CONTACT_EMAIL ? (
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, or use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
    ) : (
      <p>See the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. For privacy requests, use the <a href="/privacy/request">privacy request form</a>.</p>
    )}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
